  "summary": "Enumclaw Police are seeking three suspects who cut down two Flock-style automated license plate reader cameras early Oct. 31, leaving equipment behind. Investigators recovered video, soil impressions, and possible DNA evidence, and note similar 'deflocking' damage to eight cameras in Covington last August.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Three people in an early-2000s white, short-body cargo van cut down two automated license plate readers around 12:55 a.m. Saturday, Oct. 31, the Enumclaw Police Department said.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "People may disagree about the use of ALPR technology. That disagreement does not authorize someone with criminal intent to destroy taxpayer-funded, city-owned property.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "Cutting down the cameras is often called \"deflocking,\" and the Courier-Herald notes eight cameras were damaged in Covington last August.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    }
  ],
